      "vibe": "unsettling",
      "topic": "gaming",
      "title": "AI firms are buying and pulping millions of books",
      "caption": "Report: AI companies anonymously buying and destroying millions of physical books — for the scans. The physical copy is a licensing liability once you've got the text. We're watching the strip-mining of culture, where the artifact is destroyed to launder the data inside it.",
      "format": "tabloid",
      "bestPlatform": "bluesky",
      "triggers": [
