      "vibe": "contrarian",
      "topic": "gaming",
      "title": "Games should look worse and run better",
      "caption": "A dev's plea: the industry should ship worse-looking, better-optimised games that run on weak hardware. It's heresy in a graphics arms race — but the market it ignores (old GPUs, handhelds, the global south) is bigger than the one it's chasing. Fidelity is a tax most players didn't ask to pay.",
      "format": "quote",
      "bestPlatform": "bluesky",
      "triggers": [
        "identity",
        "participation"
      ]
    },
